course: dictionary
lesson: 8120
title: Repayment: paying money back
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A repayment is money you pay back. Look at the word parts: re- means again, pay means give money, and -ment makes it a noun, a thing. So a repayment is one payment in the paying back of a debt.
explain: «Debt becomes a problem when the repayments are more than the family can afford.» Debt and afford are clues that this is about money. Repayments means the amounts the family pays back, again and again. Swap in «paying back» to check: «when the paying back is more than the family can afford» still makes sense.
explain: In adult life, repayments are often regular amounts paid on loans, mortgages and credit cards. They usually include interest, which is extra money on top of what was borrowed. In a maths problem, a 600 dollar loan repaid in 6 repayments with no interest means 100 dollars each.
fact: A repayment is money you pay back.
fact: «Monthly repayments» are amounts paid back once a month on a loan, mortgage or car.
fact: Repayments on loans usually include interest, which is extra money.
fact: A repayment can also mean something given back for help: «in repayment for your kindness».
fact: To miss a repayment means not paying one of the amounts when it is due.
exercise: «Debt becomes a problem when the repayments are more than the family can afford.» What are the repayments? | Presents given to friends | Gifts for the school fair | *Money the family pays back on what it borrowed | Money the family spends on holidays
exercise: A 600 dollar loan is repaid in 6 equal repayments, with no interest. How much is each repayment? | 60 dollars | *100 dollars | 600 dollars | 50 dollars
exercise: What does «in repayment for your kindness» mean? | *As a thank you, giving something back for your help | A payment for a new coat | A sad, slow walk home | Being unkind again
test: A family misses a repayment. What does that mean? | They borrowed more money on purpose | They paid back the whole loan in one go | They won a prize at the bank | *They did not pay one of the amounts on a loan when it was due
test: Which phrase means regular amounts paid back on a loan each month? | Sunny weather | Happy birthdays | *Monthly repayments | Loud whispers
exam: Ravi takes a loan and must make monthly repayments. What must he do each month? | Borrow even more money | Give away his savings | *Pay back a set amount of the loan | Spend the loan on toys
